### Python Backend Guide

- **App creation**: `create_app()` in [api/app_factory.py](mdc:api/app_factory.py) initializes Flask, extensions (e.g., [api/extensions/ext_database.py](mdc:api/extensions/ext_database.py)), and blueprints (see [api/extensions/ext_blueprints.py](mdc:api/extensions/ext_blueprints.py)).
- **Config**: App config in [api/configs/app_config.py](mdc:api/configs/app_config.py); feature flags in [api/configs/feature/](mdc:api/configs/feature/); middleware config in [api/configs/middleware/](mdc:api/configs/middleware/).
- **Controllers (routes)**: Under [api/controllers/](mdc:api/controllers/):
  - console-facing: [api/controllers/console/](mdc:api/controllers/console/)
  - service APIs: [api/controllers/service_api/](mdc:api/controllers/service_api/)
  - web-sharing: [api/controllers/web/](mdc:api/controllers/web/)
- **Domain services**: Business logic in [api/services/](mdc:api/services/). Repositories in [api/repositories/](mdc:api/repositories/), SQLAlchemy models in [api/models/](mdc:api/models/).
- **Tasks/Workers**: Celery tasks in [api/tasks/](mdc:api/tasks/). Event handling in [api/events/event_handlers/](mdc:api/events/event_handlers/).
- **RAG & Workflow**: Modules at [api/core/rag/](mdc:api/core/rag/) and [api/core/workflow/](mdc:api/core/workflow/).
- **Model runtime**: Providers and runtimes at [api/core/model_runtime/](mdc:api/core/model_runtime/).

Conventions
- Prefer services → repositories → models layering.
- Validate request payloads in controllers; keep business logic in services.
- Add migrations under [api/migrations/versions/](mdc:api/migrations/versions/).

### Backend (API)

All Python commands must be prefixed with `uv run`:

```bash
# Run tests
uv run pytest      # Run all tests
uv run pytest tests/unit_tests/     # Unit tests only
uv run pytest tests/integration_tests/  # Integration tests

# Code quality
uv run ruff check --fix ./    # Fix linting issues
uv run ruff format ./         # Format code
uv run mypy .                 # Type checking
```
